\title{bushfireheat: Explore Fire-Season Heat in South-Eastern Australia}
\description{
Daily maximum temperature and rainfall from the ERA5 reanalysis for eight towns in south-eastern Australia affected by the 2019/20 Black Summer fires. Functions count hot days in each September to February fire season, compare a recent period with a mid-century baseline and plot the result, and a Shiny app lets users explore how often extreme fire-season heat now occurs and how sensitive that change is to the temperature threshold.
